<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The note reads COMPLETELY DIFFERENTLY in each language.<br />
I ran it through Google Translate and got the following:<br />
Swedish:<br />
I apologize for the trouble I've caused.<br />
It is a lie.</p>
<p>I assure two challenges, because all of you are weak:<br />
1. I will always be a lobster.<br />
2. I am sick - Please help me.</p>
<p>Worship me.</p>
<p>German:<br />
I do not appreciate the problems you brought me.<br />
I continue to learn how to exist.</p>
<p>There are only two things I can guarantee for the future:</p>
<p>1. I will always be a lobster.<br />
2. I will kill you all.</p>
<p>Go to hell.</p>
<p>English:<br />
I am sorry for the trouble that I've caused you.<br />
I'm still getting the hang of this &quot;magic&quot; thing.</p>
<p>Here are my laws:</p>
<p>1. I will always be a hermit crab.<br />
2. I am hungry.</p>
<p>Happy Thanksgiving.</p>
<p>The invisible text just says &quot;Leviticus 11:12&quot; which is basically saying that seafood without fins or scales shall be an abomination unto you, or something like that.</p>
